<title>USA: Wall Street stocks seen opening lower.</title>
<headline>Wall Street stocks seen opening lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. stocks are expected to follow through on yesterday's weak close and open lower on Friday as interest rate worries resumed their hold on investors.</p>
<p>The Dow industrials finished off about 20 points, or 0.3 percent, at 6792 on Thursday despite an early surge caused by an earnings-driven rally in shares of International Business Machines Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we ran out of steam. Interest rate worries are uppermost in people's minds, putting IBM and good earnings into the background for a little while,&quot; an analyst said.</p>
</text>
